  data: {
    LLM: "Dump your Jacks! If you can't follow suit, play your Jacks immediately to ensure an opponent captures them. Save your lowest cards (7s and 8s) for the end of the round, as this is when the 'Big Jacks' usually come out as players run out of suit-fillers.\n\nThe 'Polignac Trap': If you hold the Queen, King, or Ace of Spades, you are in danger of winning the Polignac. Try to lead Spades early in the round while everyone still has low Spades (7, 8, 9). This 'Clears' the suit and forces the person with the Jack to play it early when you aren't forced to win it.\n\nThe 'Capot' (Slam): In some house rules, if you capture ALL FOUR Jacks, you score zero points and everyone else gets 5. If you have a massive hand of high cards, you might intentionally 'Vacuum' up the Jacks to trigger this bonus. However, if you miss even one, you will have a disastrous score. It's the 'Shoot the Moon' of Polignac.",
    Player: "Dump your Jacks! If you can't follow suit, play your Jacks immediately to ensure an opponent captures them. Save your lowest cards (7s and 8s) for the end of the round, as this is when the 'Big Jacks' usually come out as players run out of suit-fillers.\n\nThe 'Polignac Trap': If you hold the Queen, King, or Ace of Spades, you are in danger of winning the Polignac. Try to lead Spades early in the round while everyone still has low Spades (7, 8, 9). This 'Clears' the suit and forces the person with the Jack to play it early when you aren't forced to win it.\n\nThe 'Capot' (Slam): In some house rules, if you capture ALL FOUR Jacks, you score zero points and everyone else gets 5. If you have a massive hand of high cards, you might intentionally 'Vacuum' up the Jacks to trigger this bonus. However, if you miss even one, you will have a disastrous score. It's the 'Shoot the Moon' of Polignac.",
